Subject: [PATCH] core: store Xbox snapshots in a dedicated qcow2

QEMU's internal snapshots need a block device that can hold vmstate. A raw
or read-only Xbox HDD cannot, so saving a state failed with "no block device
can store vmstate for snapshot". For those images the shell now provides a
dedicated qcow2 store; it is created at machine init and opened only for a
save-state request. Snapshot metadata and thumbnails are read from the selected
store, and the HDD format is explicit so a raw image is not probed.

Applies on top of the XGrid 0.8.139 tree.

diff --git a/xemu/config_spec.yml b/xemu/config_spec.yml
index 80e7661e..b05aa16d 100644
--- a/xemu/config_spec.yml
+++ b/xemu/config_spec.yml
@@ -376,7 +376,17 @@ sys:
     flashrom_path: string
     eeprom_path: string
     hdd_path: string
+    # Block format for hdd_path: auto probes, raw avoids QEMU's raw-image write
+    # restriction, qcow2 is explicit. The shell picks it from the file name.
+    hdd_format:
+      type: enum
+      values: [auto, raw, qcow2]
+      default: auto
     dvd_path: string
+    # qcow2 store for Xbox VM snapshots when the hard-disk image cannot hold
+    # them (a raw or read-only image). Empty: disabled. A qcow2 HDD keeps its
+    # snapshots inside the image.
+    snapshot_store_path: string
 
